# Schema of the box model (reference/common/structure.md).
# First the elements, then the reusable rules (Styles), the groups (Box, Typography,
# Break) and finally the properties.
# Each name has a single definition in the whole namespace: the Width of Page and the one of Box are
# the same node.
Schema (@stxt.schema): dev.stxt.pdf
	Description: Documents of stxt-pdf, the layout and PDF generation engine. Lengths are in points (12) or in millimeters (12mm). Manual in docs/en/manual and complete reference in docs/en/reference.

	# Elements

	Node: Document
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Box document: the medium (the one of the sections that do not declare their own), the title and the language (required), the reusable rules (also the base typography, with For element: Document), the Page overlay of all the sections and one or more Section with the content, in order.
		Children:
			Child: Page
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Title
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Language
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Styles
				Max: 1
			Child: Page overlay
			Child: Section
				Min: 1
	Node: Page
		Type: GROUP
		Description: The page: its size, with Paper (and Orientation) or with Width and Height, and its margins. It defines the page area, which is the initial reference container.
		Children:
			Child: Paper
				Max: 1
			Child: Orientation
				Max: 1
			Child: Width
				Max: 1
			Child: Height
				Max: 1
			Child: Margin
				Max: 1
	Node: Section
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Independent part of the document: it starts a new page and has its own Page (which inherits from the document by groups), its own Page overlay and its own page numbering. It contains the in-flow elements and the positioned ones.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Page
				Max: 1
			Child: Page numbering
				Max: 1
			Child: Page number format
				Max: 1
			Child: Start
				Max: 1
			Child: Inherit page overlays
				Max: 1
			Child: Begin on
				Max: 1
			Child: Block
			Child: Stack
			Child: Grid
			Child: Text
			Child: Paragraph
			Child: Heading 1
			Child: Heading 2
			Child: Heading 3
			Child: Heading 4
			Child: Heading 5
			Child: Heading 6
			Child: List
			Child: Markdown
			Child: Table of contents
			Child: Image
			Child: Barcode
			Child: Table
			Child: Columns
			Child: Frame
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
	Node: Block
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Box that stacks its children vertically (block flow).
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Isolate margins
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Block
			Child: Stack
			Child: Grid
			Child: Text
			Child: Paragraph
			Child: Heading 1
			Child: Heading 2
			Child: Heading 3
			Child: Heading 4
			Child: Heading 5
			Child: Heading 6
			Child: List
			Child: Markdown
			Child: Table of contents
			Child: Image
			Child: Barcode
			Child: Table
			Child: Columns
			Child: Frame
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
	Node: Stack
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Places its items (Item) one after another, horizontally or vertically (Direction), and distributes the leftover space among them.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Direction
				Max: 1
			Child: Wrap
				Max: 1
			Child: Gap
				Max: 1
			Child: Horizontal
				Max: 1
			Child: Vertical
				Max: 1
			Child: Line distribution
				Max: 1
			Child: Item
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
	Node: Grid
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Grid container: places its items (Area) in a grid of rows and columns.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Column sizes
				Max: 1
			Child: Row sizes
				Max: 1
			Child: Gap
				Max: 1
			Child: Areas
				Max: 1
			Child: Flow
				Max: 1
			Child: Horizontal
				Max: 1
			Child: Vertical
				Max: 1
			Child: Area
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
	Node: Text
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Standalone text, not a paragraph of the content: a label, a figure, a line of a header, the pieces of a heading. The text goes in the value (one line) or in Content (a block), without blank lines unless it is preformatted.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
	Node: Paragraph
		Type: INLINE
		Description: A paragraph of the content, which For element: Paragraph rules style separately from standalone texts. A single paragraph: no blank lines in Content.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
	Node: Heading 1
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Level 1 heading: a block with one or more Text. It appears in the PDF bookmarks and the engine avoids breaking inside it and after it.
