	Node: Table
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Table: its rows (Row) in Header rows, Body and Footer rows, in that order, over the columns of Column sizes. When it breaks, Header rows and Footer rows are repeated on each page.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Column sizes
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Column align
				Max: 1
			Child: Gap
				Max: 1
			Child: Header rows
				Max: 1
			Child: Body
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Footer rows
				Max: 1
	Node: Header rows
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Header rows of a Table: they go at the start of each page of the table.
		Children:
			Child: Row
				Min: 1
	Node: Body
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Body rows of a Table.
		Children:
			Child: Row
				Min: 1
	Node: Footer rows
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Footer rows of a Table: they go at the end of each page of the table.
		Children:
			Child: Row
				Min: 1
	Node: Row
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Row of a table: its cells (Cell), from left to right. It is not a layout box: its Box only accepts the appearance (Background, Border, Border color and Corner radius), which is painted as a band beneath its cells, and its Id is a link target. Its Typography is inherited by its cells, and the For style rules of its Style and For id rules of its Id apply to each of them.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Cell
				Min: 1
	Node: Cell
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Cell of a table. With a value, a one-line text box; without a value, a block with its elements (or empty).
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Span
				Max: 1
			Child: Row header
				Max: 1
			Child: Block
			Child: Stack
			Child: Grid
			Child: Text
			Child: Paragraph
			Child: List
			Child: Markdown
			Child: Table of contents
			Child: Image
			Child: Barcode
			Child: Table
			Child: Columns
			Child: Frame
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay

	Node: Markdown
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Content in Markdown (headings, paragraphs, lists, GFM tables, code blocks and, inline, **bold**, *italic*, ++underline++, ~~strikethrough~~, `code` and [links](target)), which is translated into Heading, Paragraph, List, Table and Text. A block.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Bullet markers
				Max: 1
			Child: Number markers
				Max: 1
			Child: Table columns
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
	Node: Table of contents
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Automatic table of contents: one entry per heading of the levels in Levels, in document order, with its title, a leader and the page. A block; the entries are styled with the For element rules 'TOC 1' to 'TOC 6'.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Levels
				Max: 1
			Child: Leader
				Max: 1
	Node: Image
		Type: INLINE
		Description: PNG, JPEG, SVG or PDF image from the images/ folder of the resources; the value is its path, relative to images/ (logos/acme.png). A box without children with the size and proportions of the file (of a PDF, of its page); it does not break across pages.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Alt
				Max: 1
			Child: Fit
				Max: 1
			Child: Pdf page
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
	Node: Barcode
		Type: INLINE
		Description: QR code or barcode that the engine generates from its data, in the Format qr (by default), code-128 or ean-13. The data goes in the value (Barcode: https://example.com/verify/1234) or, if it has several lines, in a Content >> block, one of the two. It is laid out as an Image: its natural size comes from its modules (0.5 mm in a QR code; 0.33 mm by 22.85 mm in the others), with the quiet zone included; a QR code is drawn square and centered, and the others are stretched to the box. Alt is required. The modules have the Color of the Typography (only Color is allowed in its Typography) and the background is that of the Box.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Alt
				Max: 1
			Child: Format
				Max: 1
			Child: Error correction
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1

	# Reusable rules

	Node: Styles
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Reusable rules: default properties of the elements of a type, with a named style or with an Id, and the colors with a name (Named color). It is a child of Document or the root of a separate styles document, which is passed along with the document and ranks below it.
		Children:
			Child: Named color
			Child: For element
			Child: For style
			Child: For id
			Child: For column
	Node: Named color
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Color with a name: the name and the color separated by a space (Named color: brand #12315A). The name, in lowercase letters and digits with words joined by hyphens, is then written wherever a color goes (Color, Border color, Background, also inside linear, and Separator color). If the document and the separate styles document declare the same name, the document wins.
	Node: For element
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Rule for all the elements of a type; the value is its name (Text, Block, Heading 1...), one generated by the engine (Code block, the code block of a Markdown; TOC 1 to 6, the entries of a Table of contents), a position within a table (Header cell, Body cell, Footer cell, Odd row cell, Even row cell) or Document, which only accepts Typography and is the typography that all boxes inherit.
		Children:
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
	Node: For style
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Rule for the elements that have that style in their Style.
		Children:
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
	Node: For id
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Rule for the element with that Id.
		Children:
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
	Node: For column
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Rule for the table cells that start in that column (n) or in any column of a range (n m, both included).
		Children:
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1

	# Groups

	Node: Box
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Box model: size, margins, padding, border and background. Not inherited.
		Children:
			Child: Width
				Max: 1
			Child: Height
				Max: 1
			Child: Min width
				Max: 1
			Child: Max width
				Max: 1
			Child: Min height
				Max: 1
			Child: Max height
				Max: 1
			Child: Aspect ratio
				Max: 1
			Child: Margin
				Max: 1
			Child: Padding
				Max: 1
			Child: Border
				Max: 1
			Child: Border color
				Max: 1
			Child: Corner radius
				Max: 1
			Child: Background
				Max: 1
	Node: Typography
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Font, code font, weight, size, line height, alignment, hyphenation, color and language of the text, heading numbering, and widows and orphans. Inherited.
		Children:
			Child: Font
				Max: 1
			Child: Code font
				Max: 1
			Child: Bold
				Max: 1
			Child: Weight
				Max: 1
			Child: Italic
				Max: 1
			Child: Size
				Max: 1
			Child: Line height
				Max: 1
			Child: Align
				Max: 1
			Child: Color
				Max: 1
			Child: Line breaking
				Max: 1
			Child: Hyphenate
				Max: 1
			Child: Markup
				Max: 1
			Child: Case
				Max: 1
			Child: Letter spacing
				Max: 1
			Child: Small caps
				Max: 1
			Child: Ligatures
				Max: 1
			Child: Kerning
				Max: 1
			Child: Preformatted
				Max: 1
			Child: Tab size
				Max: 1
			Child: Widows
				Max: 1
			Child: Orphans
				Max: 1
			Child: Language
				Max: 1
			Child: Numbered
				Max: 1
			Child: Number format
				Max: 1
			Child: Number label
				Max: 1
	Node: Break
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Page breaks: the breaks before and after the box, what is kept together and the decoration of the broken box. Not inherited.
		Children:
			Child: Before
				Max: 1
			Child: After
				Max: 1
			Child: Keep with next
				Max: 1
			Child: Keep with previous
				Max: 1
			Child: Keep together
				Max: 1
			Child: Edges
				Max: 1

	# Document

	Node: Title
		Description: Title of the document: the one the PDF viewer shows. Required.
	Node: Language
		Description: Language, as a BCP 47 tag (es, en-US, ca...). In Document, the one of the content and of the tagged PDF (required). In Typography, the one of a box whose text is in another language (inherited): a screen reader reads it (Lang of the tagged PDF) and it sets the letter rules of Case. Not valid in For element: Document, which uses the one of Document.

	# Element

	Node: Id
		Description: Identifier for dumps, tests, messages and For id rules. Unique in the document.
	Node: Style
		Description: Named styles of the element, separated by spaces: the For style rules with those names apply to it. In a Row, to each of its cells.
	Node: Link
		Description: Target the whole box leads to when clicked: https://..., http://..., mailto:... or #id (a box of the document). It does not change its appearance.
	Node: In table of contents
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the heading has an entry in the tables of contents (Table of contents). By default, true. With false it is still a heading (structure, bookmark and hierarchy) but it is not listed: the title of the cover or the one of the table of contents itself.
	Node: Isolate margins
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box isolates the margins of its children: with true, those of the first and the last stay inside and do not merge with its own. By default, false.
	Node: Offset
		Description: Offset: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Layer
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Stacking order within its context. Not declared = auto.
	Node: Pages
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Pages on which a Page overlay appears, counting from 1 within its scope (those of the document if it is a Page overlay of Document, those of the section if it is of a Section): all, every page; first, only the first; not-first, all but the first; odd, the odd ones; even, the even ones; last, only the last.
		Values:
			Value: all
			Value: first
			Value: not-first
			Value: odd
			Value: even
			Value: last
	Node: Page numbering
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How a Section numbers its pages with {page} and {pages}: continue (by default) follows the document counter, restart goes back to 1 and none neither numbers them nor advances the counter (a cover). {pages} is the last number of the page sequence, which starts at each restart.
		Values:
			Value: continue
			Value: restart
			Value: none
	Node: Page number format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the page numbers of a Section are written: decimal (1, by default), lower-roman (i) or upper-roman (I), in {page}, {pages}, {page of: id}, the tables of contents and the viewer. Not valid with Page numbering: none.
		Values:
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
	Node: Inherit page overlays
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the Section carries the Page overlay of the Document. By default, true; with false only its own appear (a cover without a footer).
	Node: Begin on
		Type: ENUM
		Description: On which physical page a Section starts: any (by default), on the next one; odd, on an odd one, the right-hand one when printing double-sided. If it does not fall there, the previous section ends with a blank page, which counts for the number but does not print it or carry the Page overlay. Not valid in the first section.
		Values:
			Value: any
			Value: odd
	Node: Rotate
		Type: NUMBER
		Description: Rotation of the box, in degrees clockwise (from -360 to 360, without 0). In Block, Text, Paragraph, Image and Barcode, which are in flow, it rotates about its center and the box takes the rectangle that encloses it rotated; without Width, it measures its content without breaking lines. In Frame, Overlay and Page overlay it rotates when painting, around Rotate origin, and does not change the layout. What is rotated must fit on the page and does not break across pages.
	Node: Rotate origin
		Description: Point around which the border box rotates with Rotate: one or two keywords out of top, bottom, left, right and center (top left, bottom...), or two measures from its top left corner, as lengths or as a percentage of its width and its height (20 50%). By default, center.
	Node: Paper
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Named paper size of the medium, in portrait: A3 (297 × 420 mm), A4 (210 × 297 mm), A5 (148 × 210 mm), A6 (105 × 148 mm), B4 (250 × 353 mm), B5 (176 × 250 mm), Letter (612 × 792 pt) or Legal (612 × 1008 pt). It is not declared with Width or Height.
		Values:
			Value: A3
			Value: A4
			Value: A5
			Value: A6
			Value: B4
			Value: B5
			Value: Letter
			Value: Legal
	Node: Orientation
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Orientation of the paper of Paper: portrait (by default) or landscape, which swaps the width and the height.
		Values:
			Value: portrait
			Value: landscape
	Node: Content
		Type: BLOCK
		Description: Block text. A single line break counts as a space; a blank line is an error, except in a preformatted Text (Preformatted: true or wrap). In a Barcode, the data, with its lines as they are.

	# Box

	Node: Width
		Description: Width of the border box (in Page, of the page).
	Node: Height
		Description: Height of the border box (in Page, of the page).
	Node: Min width
		Description: Minimum width.
	Node: Max width
		Description: Maximum width.
	Node: Min height
		Description: Minimum height.
	Node: Max height
		Description: Maximum height.
	Node: Aspect ratio
		Description: Width/height ratio (16/9 or a number): derives an auto axis from the other.
	Node: Margin
		Description: Margin: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Padding
		Description: Padding: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Border
		Description: Border width: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Border color
		Description: Border color: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 colors). By default, the Color of the text.
	Node: Corner radius
		Description: Rounded corners: top left, top right, bottom right, bottom left (1 to 4 values, number or %). Painting only: it rounds the background, the border and the clipping of an Image or a Barcode.
	Node: Background
		Description: Background, painted in the padding box: a color or a gradient linear(angle, color, color...).

	# Typography

	Node: Font
		Description: Font family, as declared by its TTF or OTF files in resources/fonts. Required in the text, own or inherited (also from Document).
	Node: Code font
		Description: Font family of the code (`code` in a text with Markup: markdown or in a Markdown, and the code blocks), as declared by its TTF or OTF files in resources/fonts; usually a monospaced one. Required if there is code, own or inherited.
	Node: Bold
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Bold: true is Weight: 700 and false, Weight: 400. By default, false. Not together with Weight in the same Typography.
	Node: Weight
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Weight of the font, from 100 (thin) to 900 (black) in steps of 100; the family needs a file with that weight in resources/fonts. By default, 400.
	Node: Italic
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Italic: the italic variant of the font. By default, false.
	Node: Size
		Description: Font size, a length. Required in the text, own or inherited (also from Document).
	Node: Line height
		Description: Line height: a length, or a percentage (120%) relative to the Size.
	Node: Align
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Alignment of the lines.
		Values:
			Value: left
			Value: right
			Value: center
			Value: justify
	Node: Color
		Description: Color of the text.
	Node: Line breaking
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Line breaking of the text: simple (greedy, by default: each line is filled as much as it can) or balanced (Knuth-Plass, which balances the lines of the paragraph).
		Values:
			Value: simple
			Value: balanced
	Node: Hyphenate
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the line breaking may split a word at the end of a line with a hyphen, following the hyphenation patterns of the language of Language (the engine has them for es, ca, en-US and en-GB; any other language is an error). By default, false. Inherited. A soft hyphen (U+00AD) in the text is always a break point, with or without Hyphenate, and is only painted where the word is split.
	Node: Markup
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Inline formatting of the text: none (by default; the text is literal) or markdown (interprets **bold**, *italic*, ++underline++, ~~strikethrough~~ and [links](target), with the CommonMark escapes; it does nothing inside a Markdown).
		Values:
			Value: none
			Value: markdown
	Node: Case
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Letter case of the text when painting it: none (by default), uppercase, lowercase or capitalize (the first letter of each word). The text of the document and the one in the PDF structure remain as written; the rules for each letter are those of the language of Language.
		Values:
			Value: none
			Value: uppercase
			Value: lowercase
			Value: capitalize
	Node: Letter spacing
		Description: Spacing between letters, a length, added to the advance of each character (also in line breaking and in justify); the last character of the line does not get it. It can be negative. By default, 0.
	Node: Small caps
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Small caps: lowercase letters are painted as uppercase at 80 % of the size. By default, false.
	Node: Ligatures
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the text is measured and painted with the ligatures of the font (fi, fl, ffi...). By default, false: one glyph per character. Inherited. With Letter spacing other than 0 there are no ligatures. It only matters in the fonts that have them (IBM Plex Sans and Serif; Plex Mono does not).
	Node: Kerning
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the text is measured and painted with the kerning pairs of the font, which adjust the space between two letters (AV, To). By default, false. Inherited. The pairs come from the kern feature of the GPOS table or, in a font without it, from the kern table; a pair does not cross a space or the boundary between two runs. It does not change the text that is read or copied.
	Node: Preformatted
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Preformatted text: false (by default; spaces and line breaks count as a space), true (keeps the spaces and line breaks, and does not break lines: one wider than the box is an error) or wrap (like true, but breaks lines that are too wide between words). Preformatted lines are not justified.
		Values:
			Value: false
			Value: true
			Value: wrap
	Node: Tab size
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: With Preformatted: true or wrap, the width of a tab: each one leads to the next column that is a multiple of this number of characters. By default, 4.
	Node: Numbered
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the headings carry a number (1, 1.1, 1.1.1...), which is written before the title and is given by {number of: id}, the tables of contents and the PDF bookmarks. By default, false. Inherited: For element: Document turns it on in all of them, a For element rule in those of one level and, in the Typography of a heading, only in that one. Headings whose Numbered is false are neither numbered nor counted.
	Node: Number format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the level number of a numbered heading is written: decimal (1, by default), lower-alpha (a), upper-alpha (A), lower-roman (i) or upper-roman (I). Each level of the full number is written with the one of its heading (II.a). Inherited.
		Values:
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-alpha
			Value: upper-alpha
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
	Node: Number label
		Description: What is written before the title of a numbered heading, with {number} where the number goes (Number label: Annex {number}.); without it, the number. Inherited.
	Node: Widows
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Minimum number of lines of a paragraph that move to the next page. By default, 2.
	Node: Orphans
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Minimum number of lines of a paragraph that stay at the end of a page. By default, 2.

	# Break

	Node: Before
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Break before the box: auto (by default) does not force it; page takes it to a new page and column, inside a Columns, to the next column.
		Values:
			Value: auto
			Value: page
			Value: column
	Node: After
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Break after the box: auto (by default) does not force it; page takes what follows to a new page and column, inside a Columns, to the next column.
		Values:
			Value: auto
			Value: page
			Value: column
	Node: Keep with next
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box is kept on the same page as the next one: it avoids the break between the two (titles, labels). By default, false. With After: page or column, it is a contradiction.
	Node: Keep with previous
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box is kept on the same page as the previous one: it avoids the break between the two. By default, false. With Before: page or column, it is a contradiction.
	Node: Keep together
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box is kept whole: it avoids breaking it across pages. By default, false.
	Node: Edges
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Border and padding of a box broken across pages: open (by default) leaves them open at the break; closed closes them in each fragment, which carries its full border and padding.
		Values:
			Value: open
			Value: closed

	# Stack

	Node: Direction
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Main axis of a Stack, along which the items go one after another: horizontal (by default) or vertical.
		Values:
			Value: horizontal
			Value: vertical
	Node: Wrap
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Allows the items to be distributed over several lines.
	Node: Gap
		Description: Spacing: in Stack and Grid, one value, or two (rows columns); in Columns, one value, the gap between columns.
	Node: Line distribution
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Distribution of the lines in the container: start, end, center, justify (the first and the last at the edges), around or stretch. Only with Wrap: true.
		Values:
			Value: start
			Value: end
			Value: center
			Value: justify
			Value: around
			Value: stretch
	Node: Grow
		Description: Share of the leftover space that the item receives.
	Node: Shrink
		Description: Share of the shortfall that the item gives up, weighted by Base size.
	Node: Base size
		Description: Starting size of the item on the main axis.

	# Grid

	Node: Column sizes
		Description: Size of each column: one track per column.
	Node: Row sizes
		Description: Size of each row: one track per row.
	Node: Areas
		Type: TEXT
		Description: One row of the grid per line; names separated by spaces and . for empty cells.
	Node: Flow
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Direction of the automatic placement of a Grid: horizontal (by default) fills the rows one by one; vertical, the columns.
		Values:
			Value: horizontal
			Value: vertical
	Node: Horizontal
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Horizontal alignment or distribution. In a Grid, the alignment of all the items in their area, and in an Area, that of one (start, end, center or stretch). In a Stack, if its main axis is the horizontal one, the distribution of the leftover space (start, end, center, justify, around or distribute); if not, the alignment of all the items (start, end, center or stretch). In an Item, the alignment of one, only if it is the cross axis of its Stack.
		Values:
			Value: start
			Value: end
			Value: center
			Value: stretch
			Value: justify
			Value: around
			Value: distribute
	Node: Vertical
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Vertical alignment or distribution, like Horizontal: in a Grid and in an Area, the alignment in the area; in a Stack, the distribution if its main axis is the vertical one and, if not, the alignment of the items; in an Item, the alignment of one, only if it is the cross axis of its Stack.
		Values:
			Value: start
			Value: end
			Value: center
			Value: stretch
			Value: justify
			Value: around
			Value: distribute

	# List

	Node: Marker
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Marker of the items: bullet (•), dash (–) or none, or a numbering (1., a., A., i., I.).
		Values:
			Value: bullet
			Value: dash
			Value: none
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-alpha
			Value: upper-alpha
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
	Node: Start
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Number a numbering starts with: that of the first item of a numbered list or, in a Section with Page numbering: restart, that of its first page. By default, 1.
	Node: Number
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Number of this item of a numbered list; the following ones continue from it.

	# Table

	Node: Span
		Description: Rows and columns the cell spans, in that order (1 1 by default): 1 3 spans three columns of its row.
	Node: Row header
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: The cell is the header of its row (the item of an invoice, the time of a timetable): in the tagged PDF it is a TH with Scope Row, and a screen reader announces it with each cell of the row. By default, false. Not valid in Header rows, whose cells are already column headers.

	# Columns

	Node: Count
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Number of columns of a Columns (at least 1); with Min column width, the maximum.
	Node: Min column width
		Description: Minimum width of the columns: as many fit as the width allows, up to Count if it is declared.
	Node: Separator
		Description: Width of the line between the columns of a Columns, centered in Gap, which must be at least as wide.
	Node: Separator color
		Description: Color of the line between columns. By default, the Color of the text.
	Node: Balance
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Distribution among the columns of a Columns: with true (by default) the columns of the last fragment are balanced; with false they are filled in order.

	# Image

	Node: Alt
		Description: Alternative text of an Image or a Barcode: with it, the image is a figure (Figure) of the tagged PDF; without it, an Image is decorative. A Barcode requires it.
	Node: Fit
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How an Image fills its box if they have different proportions: inside (by default) fits whole and centered; fill fills the box, centered and clipped; stretch stretches it to the box and distorts it.
		Values:
			Value: inside
			Value: fill
			Value: stretch
	Node: Pdf page
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Page drawn by an Image of a PDF, from 1 (by default, the first). In an image that is not a PDF, or a page the PDF does not have, it is an error.

	# Barcode

	Node: Format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Symbology of a Barcode: qr (by default), a QR code; code-128, printable ASCII characters, up to 80; ean-13, 12 digits (the check digit is added) or 13 (it is checked).
		Values:
			Value: qr
			Value: code-128
			Value: ean-13
	Node: Error correction
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Error correction of a QR code, the part of its modules that can be damaged and it can still be read: low (7 %), medium (15 %, by default), quartile (25 %) or high (30 %). In another Format, it is an error.
		Values:
			Value: low
			Value: medium
			Value: quartile
			Value: high

	# Markdown

	Node: Bullet markers
		Description: Markers of the bulleted lists (-, *, +) of a Markdown, one per nesting level (the last one serves the deeper levels): bullet, dash or none.
	Node: Number markers
		Description: Markers of the numbered lists (1., 1)) of a Markdown, one per nesting level (the last one serves the deeper levels): decimal, lower-alpha, upper-alpha, lower-roman or upper-roman.
	Node: Column align
		Description: Alignment of each column of a Table (left, center, right or justify), one per column: it is the default value of its cells, which the Styles rules and what the cell declares override.
	Node: Table columns
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Columns of the tables of a Markdown: equal, all of the same width (repeat(n, *)); auto, each according to its content (repeat(n, auto)).
		Values:
			Value: equal
			Value: auto

	# Table of contents

	Node: Levels
		Description: Heading levels listed by a Table of contents: the first and the last, from 1 to 6 (by default, 1 3).
	Node: Leader
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Leader between the title and the page of the entries of a Table of contents: dots (by default), line (a line) or none.
		Values:
			Value: dots
			Value: line
			Value: none
